# system_ext-side enforcing fixes (these domains live in system_ext and are not visible to
# the vendor policy, so they cannot go in sepolicy/vendor/tb375fc_enforcing.te).
#
# batterywarning (Lenovo /system_ext/bin/batterywarning) reads
# /sys/devices/platform/charger/BatteryNotify directly. As a system_ext/platform domain it is
# neverallow'd from battery sysfs (AOSP: platform should read battery state via the health
# HAL, not raw sysfs), so this access cannot be granted without deleting an AOSP neverallow.
# It is non-boot and benign. The correct long-term fix is re-routing the Lenovo daemon through
# the health HAL - a vendor-blob behaviour change, out of sepolicy scope. Silence the noise.
dontaudit batterywarning sysfs:file { getattr open read };
